^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-03-26 00:00] observe — the current extension exposes concepts as the only custom tree view while register information remains fragmented across hover and code-lens text.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:01] observe — runtime trial data already exists in the LSP context, which makes register exploration feasible without inventing a second runtime path.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:02] decide — keep the first slice tree-based and command-driven; avoid webviews until the workspace proves a tree surface is insufficient.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:03] hygiene — base reference recorded at `main@f42a80fa8eefb813992e21f7461c96926f033416`; `main...HEAD` shows no unrelated committed drift.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:04] hygiene — local drift is present in `extensions/vscode-spw/src/annotation-index.ts`, `extensions/vscode-spw/src/extension.ts`, and `packages/spw-lsp/src/stdio-server.ts`; feature implementation should isolate that work before commit 1.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:05] taste — register state should read like a workspace object model, not a debug dump.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:06] revise — extend the interaction slice to cover resonance across files, focused graph queries around selected registers, and rotation between phase/provenance/resonance perspectives.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:07] revise — relax the plan from atlas-first sequencing to additive composition. The explorer now needs a solo-ship path from active-file snapshots, with atlas/authoring integrations layered on when those capabilities exist.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:08] observe — runtime-telemetry-canon (ready-for-commit) adds immutable substrate events, resonances, and register metadata to runSpw() results. This is the primary data source for rich register snapshots. Without it, snapshots are shallow value dumps.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:09] decide — acknowledge runtime-telemetry-canon as a cross-theme enrichment, not a blocker. Solo-ship from basic runtime trial; enrich with full telemetry when available.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:10] observe — two "phase" axes exist: spirit-sequence (?~@&*^) describes operator semantics; pipeline (lex, parse, semantic, optimize, pragmatic) describes runtime enrichment timing. register-phase-evolution plan aligns the pipeline vocabulary.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:11] decide — in the explorer tree, unqualified "phase" means pipeline phase. Detail view shows both axes when both are available. Solo-ship uses spirit-sequence phase from SIGIL_SEMANTICS; pipeline phase added when register-phase-evolution lands.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:12] observe — stdio-server.ts is 900+ lines. Adding handlers/runtime.ts needs a handler registration substrate to avoid merge bottleneck. Interaction contract now specifies this.
 >>[2026-03-27 18:00] revise — rooted into register-bank.spw, literate-ui.spw, runtime RegisterBank, type-affinities, Substrate, and interaction contract. Added parallel_work (LSP hosts transport, atlas provides manifest scope, authoring provides phase context, telemetry enriches snapshots), supporting_documents, interaction_depth, and cognitive_surface_stack. This plan operates at the substrate layer: the register tree reads register-bank SIGIL_SEMANTICS for phase grouping, acoustic properties (liminality/frequency/coupling) from register-bank spec, materialization detail from literate-architecture stages, and resonance from Substrate event channels. Each operator register backs a literate-ui navigation-primitive component — the explorer is where that mapping becomes inspectable.
}

